	(text "AUXILIARY: Pack V, both 2S packs (on when USB is absent)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "668318b2-58d8-48e1-a501-f44704275165")
	)
	(text "How it works (TI datasheet section 8.2.5, Figure 8-10, option 1):\n  USB-C is the priority input. While VUSB_PROT is inside its UVLO/OVLO window, U2 drives\n  AUXOFF (PMUX_USB_ACTIVE) high, which holds U3's OVLO pin high and keeps the battery path off.\n  When USB leaves the window, AUXOFF drops and U3 turns on within tSWOV = 90 us.\n  Both parts block reverse current, so the sources are never shorted together.\n  PMUX_USB_ACTIVE and PMUX_BAT_ACTIVE also tell the MCU which source is powering UNREG.\n\nCalculations (resistors 1%):\n  USB UVLO   383k/147k: on at 1.20 x 530/147 = 4.33 V, off at 1.09 x 530/147 = 3.93 V\n  USB OVLO   590k/147k: off above 1.20 x 737/147 = 6.02 V, back on below 5.46 V\n  Pack UVLO  412k/100k: on at 1.20 x 5.12 = 6.14 V, off at 1.09 x 5.12 = 5.58 V (2.8 V/cell)\n  Current limit  R_ILM = 3334 / I_LIM: 1.13k -> 2.95 A (load is 1.5-2 A per #170; R_ILM >= 750R)\n  dVdt 3.3 nF: 2000 / 3300 pF = 0.61 V/ms, 8.4 V in 14 ms, inrush into 220 uF = 133 mA\n  ITIMER 2.2 nF: 1.51 V x 2.2 nF / 1.8 uA = 1.8 ms of allowed overcurrent before limiting\n  Switchover dip, USB -> pack: 90 us x 2 A / 220 uF = 0.82 V below the 3.93 V USB UVLO\n    off point, so UNREG dips to about 3.1 V\n  Loss: 2 A^2 x 28 mOhm = 0.11 W per part\n  AUXOFF pull-ups 220k: with U2 unpowered (flight, no USB) its AUXOFF floats up to 1.0 V at\n    26 uA (VPGD). 12 uA keeps it lower, below U3's 1.183 V OVLO and an MCU's 0.3 x VDD low.\n    Asserted high with 3 uA max leakage: 3.3 V - 0.66 V = 2.64 V, above 0.7 x VDD.\n  Cap ratings: dVdt caps need the higher rail + 5 V = 13.4 V (datasheet note), so 25 V.\n    Input caps are 1 uF at 2x the input voltage (datasheet 8.3.1), so 25 V.\n    C8 is polymer tantalum, not wet aluminum (vents in vacuum). 25 V is 50% derating on 8.4 V.\n    The 7343-43 footprint is a placeholder until a part is picked.\n\nFrom the EPS V2 block diagram: the inputs are Pack V (two 2S 18650 packs, 6.0-8.4 V, already\n  combined by per-pack ideal diodes) and USB-C ground power. The output is the Unreg bus, which\n  feeds the 3.3 V and 5 V regulators and rail r6.\n\nOpen questions for Ethan:\n  - Is a 5.58 V pack cutoff right, or does the charger/fuel gauge handle over-discharge?\n  - Can the #174 regulators ride through a 3.1 V dip? If not, raise the hold-up cap.\n  - Net names VUSB_PROT (#141) and PACK_V (#175) need to match those sheets.\n  - The RPW symbol and footprint aren't in the shared library yet. The symbol is embedded here.\n  - On USB power UNREG is about 5 V. Is the #174 5 V regulator a buck-boost? A buck can't\n    regulate 5 V from it.\n  - Raise the USB UVLO off point to about 4.4 V? That also shrinks the switchover dip.\n  - Does the USB-C input need a TVS (datasheet 8.3.1)?\n  - U2 AUXOFF pulls up to +3V3, which comes after this mux. At a cold start with both\n    sources present, both paths conduct (diode-OR) until 3V3 is up, then the pack turns off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6ec02e05-0e00-406b-b8dc-5259c30197de")
	)
